{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:17356555 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:17356555 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"17356555","source":"MED","pmid":"17356555","doi":"10.1038/sj.ejcn.1602718","title":"Prevention of antibiotic-associated diarrhoea by a fermented probiotic milk drink.","authorString":"Wenus C, Goll R, Loken EB, Biong AS, Halvorsen DS, Florholmen J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Wenus C","lastName":"Wenus","firstName":"C","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Clinical Nutrition, University Hospital of North Norway, Tromsoe, Norway. catrin@wenus.net"}]}},{"fullName":"Goll R","lastName":"Goll","firstName":"R","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4375-0509"}},{"fullName":"Loken EB","lastName":"Loken","firstName":"E B","initials":"EB"},{"fullName":"Biong AS","lastName":"Biong","firstName":"A S","initials":"AS"},{"fullName":"Halvorsen DS","lastName":"Halvorsen","firstName":"D S","initials":"DS"},{"fullName":"Florholmen J","lastName":"Florholmen","firstName":"J","initials":"J"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4375-0509"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"2","volume":"62","journalIssueId":1505525,"dateOfPublication":"2008 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2008,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Eur J Clin Nutr","title":"European journal of clinical nutrition","essn":"1476-5640","issn":"0954-3007","isoabbreviation":"Eur J Clin Nutr","nlmid":"8804070"},"printPublicationDate":"2008-02-01"},"pubYear":"2008","pageInfo":"299-301","abstractText":"<h4>Objective</h4>To study the preventive effect of a milk drink fermented with multistrain probiotics on antibiotic associated diarrhoea (AAD).<h4>Design</h4>Double-blind placebo controlled study.<h4>Setting</h4>University Hospital of North Norway.<h4>Subjects and methods</h4>Of 853 patients treated with antibiotics, 87 met the inclusion criteria, and were randomized to ingestion of a fermented milk drink containing LGG, La-5 and Bb-12 (n=46) or placebo with heat-killed bacteria (n=41), during a period of 14 days. A diary was recorded, and stool samples were collected for microbiological analyses.<h4>Results</h4>Sixty-three patients completed the study according to the protocol; two patients (5.9%) in the treatment group and eight (27.6%) in the placebo group developed AAD (P=0.035). The relative risk of developing AAD was 0.21 (95% confidence interval: 0.05-0.93) when given probiotic milk drink.<h4>Conclusion</h4>A fermented multistrain probiotic milk drink may prevent four of five cases of AAD in adult hospitalized patients.<h4>Sponsorship</h4>TINE BA, Oslo, Norway.","affiliation":"Department of Clinical Nutrition, University Hospital of North Norway, Tromsoe, Norway. catrin@wenus.net","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Feces","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MI","qualifierName":"microbiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bifidobacterium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GD","qualifierName":"growth & development"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Lactobacillus acidophilus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GD","qualifierName":"growth & development"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Diarrhea","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_Y